  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "Register numbers are hex and sent unchanged (2520H is sent as 25 20; the 03H example reads 01 23). Parameters map group to the high byte and number to the low byte (11-44 = 0B2CH), except 12-00 which is 32-bit at 2510H (high word) / 2511H (low word)."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "A510 Communication Addendum Modbus RTU/ASCII",
  "doc_number": "DOCUMENT-TECO-A510-AC001 Ver01",
  "revision_date": "2015-04",
  "url": "https://tecowestinghouse.com/PDF/A510_comm_addendum.pdf",
  "pages": "pp. 1-1 to 1-4 (connection, frames, exceptions), p. 1-5 (command data), pp. 1-6 to 1-8 (monitor data), parameter registers from p. 1-13"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Frequency registers are 0.01 Hz, but the addendum says resolution becomes 0.1 Hz when the motor's maximum output frequency is above 300 Hz.",
  "The addendum does not name the drive parameters for node address, baud rate, parity or run/frequency source; set those per the A510 manual.",
  "2521H (faults) and 2528H (warnings) are code tables, mapped as enums; empty table cells are omitted.",
  "Left out: 2505H and 252AH AO1 command/readback (raw scale not stated), 2506H AO2 command, 2507H DO and 2529H digital output state (no bit list).",
  "Parameter 12-00 is 32-bit (2510H high word, 2511H low word) and is not listed."
 ],
